      "text": "**\n\n1. **Understand the given equation:**\n   The given equation is $\\frac{x^2}{99} - \\frac{y^2}{36} = 1$. This is the standard form of a hyperbola centered at the origin and aligned with the coordinate axes.\n\n2. **Identify the key components:**\n   Comparing the given equation to the standard form $\\frac{x^2}{a^2} - \\frac{y^2}{b^2} = 1$:\n   - $a^2 = 99$\n   - $b^2 = 36$\n\n3. **Calculate $a$ and $b$:**\n   - $a$ is the square root of $a^2$: \n     $a = \\sqrt{99}$\n   - $b$ is the square root of $b^2$: \n     $b = \\sqrt{36} = 6$\n\n4. **Calculate the distance between the vertices:**\n   The vertices of the hyperbola are located at $(\\pm a, 0)$ in the x-direction. Therefore, the distance between the vertices is $2a$.\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance} = 2a\n   \\]\n\n5. **Substitute $a$:**\n   Since $a = \\sqrt{99}$, the distance becomes:\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance} = 2 \\cdot \\sqrt{99}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Simplify the square root:**\n   Recognize that $99 = 11^2$, so:\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance} = 2 \\cdot \\sqrt{11^2} = 2 \\cdot 11 = 22\n   \\]\n\n7. **Conclusion:**\n   Thus, the distance between the vertices of the hyperbola is $22$.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{22}\n\\]",
